{"format":1,"key":"zone:tirisfal","path":"/lore/zone/tirisfal","name":"Tirisfal Glades","kind":"zone","label":"Zone","zone":{"key":"tirisfal","name":"Tirisfal Glades","path":"/lore/zone/tirisfal"},"levels":"Levels 1-10","description":"Tirisfal Glades is the haunting northern territory of Lordaeron, now serving as the heartland of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken. Beneath…","intro":[],"clips":[{"id":"zone:tirisfal","part":"narration","anchor":"story","title":"The story","paras":["Tirisfal Glades is the haunting northern territory of Lordaeron, now serving as the heartland of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken. Beneath blighted skies and rotting boughs lie fallen manors, dormant crypts, and the vast underground capital of the Undercity. Surrounded by mindless Scourge and zealous Scarlet crusaders, it is a perilous realm where free-willed undead carve out their survival.","Once the fertile cradle of humanity, Tirisfal Glades has withered beneath the curse of the Lich King's plague. The sun rarely penetrates the murky gloom, casting an eternal sickly pale over dying woods, neglected pumpkin patches, and cold coastal hills. While remnants of old farmsteads like the Agamand Mills and Balnir Farmstead remain, their former masters have largely been swept into mass graves or risen as restless dead. Despite the devastation, a dark resilience permeates the countryside, anchored by towns like Brill and the cloistered sanctuary of Deathknell, where freshly awakened Forsaken learn to endure their second life.","Though Lady Sylvanas claims dominion over the region from the subterranean Ruins of Lordaeron, the Forsaken remain embattled on all sides. Residual Scourge thralls still infest hollows, fields, and dilapidated crypts, entirely subservient to the frozen throne of Northrend. To the east, the fanatical Scarlet Crusade has made northern Tirisfal its primary bastion, operating out of the Scarlet Monastery. Zealously devoted to the extermination of every undead creature, living and unliving alike, their outposts and patrols wage constant guerrilla warfare against Forsaken scouts and civilian travelers.","Long before human kingdoms crowned their first monarchs, the Glades bore an ancient legacy. High elven exiles briefly tried to settle these woods before shadowy energies deep beneath the earth began driving them mad, prompting their migration north. In later centuries, the secret mortal cabal known as the Council of Tirisfal chose these shadowed groves to empower solitary Guardians, shielding Azeroth from demonic intrusion."],"hash":"99d507","voices":{"male-narrator":{"sha":"329d7bbaf4","sec":128},"female-narrator":{"sha":"32994f0944","sec":132}}}],"sources":[{"kind":"wiki","title":"Tirisfal Glades (Classic)","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Tirisfal_Glades_(Classic)"},{"kind":"wiki","title":"Tirisfal Glades","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Tirisfal_Glades"}],"related":[{"p":"/lore/zone/undercity","n":"Undercity","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/zone/ruinsoflordaeron","n":"Ruins of Lordaeron","k":"dungeon"},{"p":"/lore/zone/scarlet","n":"Scarlet Monastery","k":"dungeon"},{"p":"/lore/zone/silverpine","n":"Silverpine Forest","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/zone/westernplaguelands","n":"Western Plaguelands","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/brill","n":"Brill","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/deathknell","n":"Deathknell","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/bulwark","n":"Bulwark","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/agamand-family-crypt","n":"Agamand Family Crypt","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/balnir-farmstead","n":"Balnir Farmstead","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/bandarion-keep","n":"Bandarion Keep","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/brightwater-lake","n":"Brightwater Lake","k":"subzone"}],"children":[{"p":"/lore/subzone/agamand-family-crypt","n":"Agamand Family Crypt","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/agamand-mills","n":"Agamand Mills","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/balnir-farmstead","n":"Balnir Farmstead","k":"subzone"},{"